--- a/PROVENANCE.md
+++ b/PROVENANCE.md
@@ -185,3 +185,49 @@ source-tree symlinks and special files remain rejected before cloning. The
 checkpoint-derived `storage/clone_darwin.go` is unchanged. Native CI separately
 requires two-child isolation, allocated-byte evidence, clean release, and
 daemon restart recovery on APFS and reflink-enabled XFS.
+
+## HoneyBee external Bee overlay
+
+The local `external-bee-dag-v1` integration extends the parent key, native
+parent/child lifecycle, broker negotiation and private-cache accounting.
+The immutable VHDX and Bee seed are published by one bundle rename. New Bee
+implementation and tests are additive files, not checkpoint-derived source.
+The original 42-entry frozen manifest stays unchanged; the destination overlay
+now contains 21 entries, including the changed compatibility key. This local
+patch has not been published as an upstream revision. HoneyBee records its
+base commit and exact patch SHA-256 in its packaging overlay manifest.
+
+## HoneyBee private Bee compression follow-up (2026-09-09)
+
+The hb12 overlay enables native NTFS compression only on newly seeded private
+Bee data before granting client write access. The complete tree is pinned and
+validated before mutation. Existing retained caches, immutable parent seeds,
+VHDX containers and compatibility keys are unchanged. Added native tests cover
+content/accounting, inheritance, hard-link rejection and mixed compressed/plain
+retained lifecycle behavior. The complete reviewable overlay is SHA-256 pinned
+by HoneyBee; frozen extraction manifests remain unchanged.
+
+## HoneyBee active parent recovery follow-up (2026-09-19)
+
+The hb14 overlay protects matching service-owned parent sessions from periodic
+pending recovery, including while the begin CLI has exited or Finalize is still
+running. Journal creation/session registration is serialized with the recovery
+snapshot. Native finalization does not block recovery. Protection ends after
+successful publication/abort or broker restart; abandoned in-memory sessions
+are conservatively retained rather than reclaimed using only a client PID.
+Restarted brokers retain the existing orphan quarantine rules. No on-disk schema,
+capacity floor, timeout, or compatibility key changes are made. The destination
+overlay now has 23 entries, including the additive recovery implementation and
+regression tests; the original 42-entry manifest remains unchanged.
+
+## HoneyBee commit observation follow-up (hb15, 2026-09-19)
+
+Adds authenticated, uncached read-only observations bound to broker instance,
+commit request and transaction IDs. Observations report actual worker checkpoint
+sequence and phase separately from service responsiveness, and return cached
+completion only for the matching transaction. Synchronous commit handling and
+pipe-server maintenance drain semantics are retained. Bee and VHDX checkpoints
+do not remove any sync, identity, digest or publication checks. The destination
+overlay has 25 entries with observation implementation and regression tests;
+the original frozen manifest is unchanged. This is a local, not native-qualified,
+HoneyBee overlay, not an upstream release.
